    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## H3 Video Upsampler: upscale a finished clip\n\n1. **Load Video**: pick the clip (put it in `ComfyUI/input`). Any size; 24 fps is what H3\n   assumes, other rates work but the soundtrack conditions the re-draw loosely.\n2. **Queue.** H3 Save Video writes it to `video/H3_upsampled` at the clip's own fps,\n   with its own soundtrack untouched (NVENC when there is a GPU). Set its `frame_gen` to x2 for\n   double the frame rate (RTX GPU + `nvidia-vfx`).\n\n### The node\n- **megapixels**: output size, aspect kept (2 = about 1920x1080).\n- **denoise**: as the chain's upsample_denoise. 0.2 is the original recipe (one re-draw step from sigma 0.75); 0 only enlarges.\n- **lora**: retired and ignored. The re-draw runs the original recipe with no LoRA.\n- **tile_tokens**: VRAM. Lower = more, smaller tiles, slower, less memory. 70000 is the\n  recipe; try 40000 or 25000 on a smaller card.\n- **audio_vae** wired = the re-draw hears the soundtrack; unwired = it hears silence.\n\nMouths and motion come from the clip; only fine detail is re-drawn."
   ]
  },
